\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% TRANSFORMATION TNoTopicCleft
< m1: CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}[mu1]
>

< m : CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}[mu1]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       m1: CLAUSErec1.finiteness <> finite OR
           CLAUSErec1.deixis = omegadeixis OR
           CLAUSErec1.superdeixis <> omegadeixis OR
           NOT EXIST (mu1, [I1:shiftrel/T1]) 
       I1: T1.CAT IN [NP, ADVP, PREPP] WITH T1.REC.mood = nowh
           (* more restrictive conditions will be needed *)
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TNoTopicCleft
\item[* relevant examples:] What he did see?, He did see nothing
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] CLAUSEtoSENTENCE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_TopicCleft
\item[* date of creation:] 4-OCT-1989 15:45:19  
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:]
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] to let structures in which there is no topicalized element pass 
this transformation class. 
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) The rule is NOT 
the exact counterpart of TMoveTopic: no condition is given here on the position 
of the shiftrel, so that any structure which has a shiftrel/nowh which is not 
in initial position will pass neither of the two rules. Of course, such a 
structure should not occur anyway, so that is not thought a disadvantage.
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
